From: yasoteien <263659156+yasoteien@users.noreply.github.com>
Subject: [PATCH] ARM: hibernate: Flush the TLB after switching to the identity mapping

Switch to the identity mapping and flush the TLB, as __soft_restart()
does. idmap_pgd was copied from init_mm before mark_rodata_ro(), so it
still maps the kernel text and rodata writable, but global TLB
entries left from the old page tables may still say read-only.
Copying over such a page faults with IRQs off and the restore hangs.

Signed-off-by: yasoteien <263659156+yasoteien@users.noreply.github.com>
---
--- a/arch/arm/kernel/hibernate.c	2026-11-03 18:33:51.865044844 +0900
+++ b/arch/arm/kernel/hibernate.c	2026-11-03 18:33:51.893044338 +0900
@@ -82,7 +82,15 @@
 {
 	struct pbe *pbe;
 
-	cpu_switch_mm(idmap_pgd, &init_mm);
+	/*
+	 * Switch to the identity mapping and flush the TLB, as
+	 * __soft_restart() does.  idmap_pgd was copied from init_mm before
+	 * mark_rodata_ro(), so it still maps the kernel text and rodata
+	 * writable, but global TLB entries left from the old page tables may
+	 * still say read-only.  Copying over such a page faults with IRQs off
+	 * and the restore hangs.
+	 */
+	setup_mm_for_reboot();
 	for (pbe = restore_pblist; pbe; pbe = pbe->next)
 		copy_page(pbe->orig_address, pbe->address);
 
